{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/922891-born-of-wolves","id":922891,"title":"Born of Wolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-28T15:47:30-07:00","id":922891,"title":"Born of Wolves","content":"So this hasn't been a thing since Apocalypse for obvious reasons, but it came up in a game recently and I think it can have value as a source of pathos and interest.<br /> <br /> Certain players might interpret this badly, so only introduce it if you think your players can appreciate the themes. <hr /><br /> <br /> All know that the nature of a werewolf is found in two parts - the human and the wolf. Those people born of the blood of Mother Wolf carry within them the spark that can be fanned into the flame of a mighty creature of spirit and flesh.<br /> <br /> Many have forgotten, however, that humans are not the only ones who carry the memory of Urfarah in their veins.<br /> <br /> Every now and then, humans and werewolves will run into wolves who seem more intelligent than expected. In the wild, wolves can already plan hunts, and ecologists have observed them planning weeks in advance, but the moon-blooded take that a step beyond. They come to understand the ways of nature and even humanity on a deep level. Packs with moon-blooded wolves find themselves becoming more successful at the same time that they become more subtle as their intelligent members steer them clear of danger.<br /> <br /> Where the Moon-Blooded come from is a mystery to most. Some remark that many wolf-blooded seem to come from no where at all, orphans adopted by wolf or moon. Lunacy doesn't affect wolves, but perhaps some other event shocks a part of humanity's brilliance into them. Some others, in hushed voices, whisper of the shame of Predator Kings and Forsaken long detached from humanity and too long embedded among their foreign kin.<br /> According to the Wolf-born themselves, they believe that humans are descended from werewolves, not the other way around. That there is no real evidence for this idea fails to stop the stories from popping up.<br /> <br /> Whatever the case, moon-blooded wolves possess Tells of their own, increased intelligence, and, under the right circumstances, can Change.<br /> <br /> Moon-blooded are already wolves, they already understand Rage. When a moon-blooded undergoes her First Change, it isn't in a bloody rampage, but a spark of curiosity. Where humans need to embrace the wolf inside, the wolf needs to embrace the human. They risk their lives to enter human communities, wandering into malls or schools with a painful, agonizing need to KNOW, to understand mysteries of language and technology and concepts that have haunted them and teased at the edge of their ken all their lives. When they finally understand, when the first words of meaning and knowledge spill from their lips, when their body twists and changes into a human's so they can speak to a spirit or grasp some artifact, that is the moment they become whole at last.<br /> <br /> The Lunacy inflicted by this event is interesting, causing those severely afflicted to experience painful hallucinations and haunting dreams as the moon's madness lurks in their subconscious minds. They may become inspired, or else lost in tunnels of delusion.<br /> <br /> Assuming the newly Changed werewolf survives her experience, she is no different than her human-born kin, aside from peculiarities that come from an alien upbringing. She may speak First Tongue with a grace that her kin could envy, and has trouble initially with human languages, though if she's interacted extensively with humans or werewolves in the past this might not be the case.<br /> <br /> Most gain the <b>Wolf-born</b> Persistent Condition:<br /> Born of wolves rather than humans, this werewolf has little background in language or basic concepts that even the most deprived human finds second nature, but possesses a strong grasp in the instinctive nature of spirits and the wild. Lose 10-again on Mental skills and social rolls with humans, gain 9-again on rolls involving animals, natural settings, Intimidation, or in understanding and interacting with spirits. On a failure in social rolls, the wolf-born automatically resorts to growls and vocalizations.<br /> <b>Beat</b>: When substantially inconvenienced by an unfamiliarity with social norms or technology.<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Substantial socialization and teaching in human concepts.<br /> <br /> <br /> When creating a Moon-blooded wolf, simply create a normal Mortal character, then select a Tell. Moon-blooded have access to appropriate merits available to Wolf-blooded. Apply the form bonus for being Urhan.<br /> Tells available to the Moon-blooded tend to have &quot;opposite&quot; effects where available, and some may be inappropriate and demand custom Tells. For instance, Liar's Skin is fairly invalid and Wolf Skin is a bit weird, though there can be variations on them, but ones like Anger Issues and Spirit Double can be used without issue. When a Tell would give Dalu form, it instead grants Urshul form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":5226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","user":"Jachra","date":". 07-05-2016, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T16:05:12-07:00","id":922898,"title":"","content":"Cool cool. There have been a couple recent discussions on this topic so if you want to find like-minded people you can find them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken/page2\">Here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/914222-forsaken-youths\">here</a> I guess.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T16:59:29-07:00","id":922920,"title":"","content":"Never liked the \u201cwolves are spiritual\u201d thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T17:20:08-07:00","id":922932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/922891-born-of-wolves?p=922920#post922920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never liked the \u201cwolves are spiritual\u201d thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits are fairly animalistic, with single-minded purposes based around feeding, which I think a wolf-born would understand. They also tend to live in natural areas with weak Gauntlets, so they would have a great deal of experience with spirits as a matter of course. If they're living in an area with a strong Gauntlet, they're almost certainly being socialized, and so don't get that Condition.<br /> I think it would be legitimate to remove it, mind, if you prefer.<br /> <br /> I've read your earlier post now, and I think Moon-Blooded might be a better term than Dire Wolf, regardless which ruleset you go with - Dire Wolves refers to a species of extinct wolf that is fairly massive, and urhanu aren't massive unless they have the Tell that lets them become Urshul, and then only temporarily, where as Moon-Blooded is a logical mirror counterpart to Wolf-Blooded.<br /> <br /> I think your rules in your section are perfectly acceptable, though, with one exception - I don't know that they should get free dots in skills or specialties. Just design them as normal Werewolves, if they player isn't putting dots in Survival and Animal Ken, then they really should have some reason why not.<br /> <br /> I'd like to include some of your comments about Tells, certainly, and maybe adjust my Condition accordingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-28T20:56:27-07:00","id":923043,"title":"","content":"Go right ahead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T13:33:08-07:00","id":923452,"title":"","content":"Just a side note: A wolf-born Werewolf should probably start with Harmony 3 instead of Harmony 7.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T15:57:27-07:00","id":923539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/922891-born-of-wolves?p=923452#post923452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a side note: A wolf-born Werewolf should probably start with Harmony 3 instead of Harmony 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's like 2 Bans deep, not counting Totemic ones. Kinda iffy on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T16:06:15-07:00","id":923542,"title":"","content":"I'd really say they were still at 7, providing they joined a tribe and everything. It's flesh to spirit, not human to wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T16:33:23-07:00","id":923559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/922891-born-of-wolves?p=923452#post923452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a side note: A wolf-born Werewolf should probably start with Harmony 3 instead of Harmony 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're beings of flesh, not spirit. They would almost certainly start with 9 if freshly changed from moon-blooded or 7 if created normally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T01:09:30-07:00","id":923755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/922891-born-of-wolves?p=923452#post923452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a side note: A wolf-born Werewolf should probably start with Harmony 3 instead of Harmony 7.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Jachra said. Wolf-born Harmony should start same as humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T01:31:53-07:00","id":923760,"title":"","content":"Wolves being more &quot;spiritual&quot; makes a hell of a lot more sense in Forsaken than it ever did in Apocalypse, given the universally predatory nature of the Hisil.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T02:51:49-07:00","id":923772,"title":"","content":"The most successful predators in the world, possibly of all time, are humans. This argument about 'spiritual' therefore doesn't work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T03:06:01-07:00","id":923776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/922891-born-of-wolves?p=923772#post923772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most successful predators in the world, possibly of all time, are humans. This argument about 'spiritual' therefore doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But overwhelmingly we don't live &quot;hunt or die&quot; lives. So no, not buying that argument. Those societies that are built around hunting for survival, tend to have belief systems closer to what is objectively correct in the world of WtF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-30-2016, 06:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T03:23:28-07:00","id":923781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/922891-born-of-wolves?p=923776#post923776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> But overwhelmingly we don't live &quot;hunt or die&quot; lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not right now, no. But we did. And there's nothing suggesting that ancient werewolves started with Harmony more closely aligned to spirit than flesh.<br /> <br /> Wolves also don't just hunt other wolves for prey. Spirits do. You know who also overwhelmingly hunts and kills their own kind to increase their power? Humans.<br /> <br /> The hunt = spiritual argument isn't a good one. Arguably, a wolf suddenly seeing the <i>Hisil</i> would be *horrified*. Here creatures prey on their own kind. Even the spirits of prey hunt each other and can theoretically hunt their natural predators if they choose. The <i>Hisil</i> is nothing like the natural world, it's the natural order gone mad. It's alien and *wrong* to a wolf's sensibilities.<br /> <br /> But again, you know who upsets a natural order to suit themselves? Humans.<br /> <br /> Humans are probably closer to the spiritual world than anything else. They don't have reflections*, but they have more access to the spiritual than almost any other creature. How? Various merits give limited access to the spirit worlds, merits that animals and non-humans don't get. A not insignificant number of humans Awaken. They gain access to the realms beyond, while still being fundamentally human. Nothing else gains this gift.<br /> <br /> Frankly, creatures of the physical world who become werewolves start unbalanced towards flesh because they are creatures of flesh. They're not spirits, and they don't tend to have experience with the spiritual.<br /> <br /> But if you want some creature to be closer to the spirit worlds than any other, a quite reasonable argument can be made that this creature should be humans.<br /> <br /> *Why don't humans have a spiritual reflection? Is it because they are originally escapees from the spirit worlds who moved en masse to the physical world? Why else do humans have souls wrapped in flesh, whereas other creatures don't? Is every other creature less spiritual because its soul is on one side of the Gauntlet, while its flesh exists on the other?<br /> <br /> Just musing, but it's food for thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 06-30-2016, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T04:26:48-07:00","id":923786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/922891-born-of-wolves?p=923776#post923776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But overwhelmingly we don't live &quot;hunt or die&quot; lives. So no, not buying that argument. Those societies that are built around hunting for survival, tend to have belief systems closer to what is objectively correct in the world of WtF.</div> </div> </div> </div>Either do spirits. At a certain point they have a tithe system. Spirits stop being like animals once they hit Rank 2. Unless they're animal spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T09:54:08-07:00","id":923917,"title":"","content":"Also consider Breaking Points: do the activities that a wolf engages in tend to break toward Spirit or Flesh?<br /> <br /> As for creating moon-blooded wolves: not applying Urhan attribute modifiers works well enough as long as the moon-blooded never undergoes the First Change nor develops a shapeshifting Tell; but in those cases, having your character's attributes normalized to the Urhanu form complicates matters. Just for consistency and simplicity, you're probably better off selecting your attributes based on what they would be in Hishu form and then applying the Urhanu form adjustments in full.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 06-30-2016, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}